Platform: one-socket Xeon CPU Max 9480 in HBM flat mode with SNC4, HBM not yet
onlined: NUMA nodes 0-3 hold the CPUs and the DDR5; the four HBM ranges are EFI
soft-reserved memory, exposed as dax0.0-dax3.0 bound to device_dax.

Sources (kernel paths are Linux v6.18 (torvalds/linux tag v6.18)):
- Flat mode boots HBM as soft-reserved dax devices (dax0.0-dax7.0 on 2S SNC4, so
  dax0.0-dax3.0 on 1S), onlined with daxctl reconfigure-device -m system-ram, or at
  boot with efi=nosoftreserve: Intel Xeon CPU Max Series Configuration and Tuning
  Guide 354227-003 section 5.2,
  https://cdrdv2-public.intel.com/787743/354227-intel-xeon-cpu-max-series-configuration-and-tuning-guide-rev3.pdf
- /sys/bus/dax/devices/daxX.Y: Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-dax.
- Driver names device_dax (devdax mode) and kmem (system-ram mode): drivers/dax/Makefile
  module names, used as the driver name by dax_driver_register() (drivers/dax/bus.h,
  bus.c __dax_driver_register: drv->name = mod_name).
- daxctl --mode=system-ram / --mode=devdax --force: pmem/ndctl
  Documentation/daxctl/daxctl-reconfigure-device.txt (EXAMPLES).
- cpu family 6, model 143 (0x8F): arch/x86/include/asm/intel-family.h.
- SNC, cpulists, amx_*, rdt_a: as in xeon-max-hbm.

Layout: exactly the form tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes.

Not from hardware: everything xeon-max-hbm lists, plus the dax devices' parent
(devices/platform/hmem.<N>, the hmem platform devices of drivers/dax/hmem) and their
numbering, inferred from the guide, not captured.
